# Obsidian Volt Color Palette

ChessHub uses a high-tech dark theme: deep slate for trust/security, electric cyan for intelligence and modernity. Do not invent ad-hoc colors — extend tokens in `src/lib/styles/variables/_colors.scss` and mirror semantics in `src/routes/layout.css` / `tokens.scss`.

## Token map (Tailwind aliases only)

| Role | Token | Tailwind |
|------|--------|----------|
| Canvas | `$color-bg` | `slate-950` |
| Panel | `$color-surface` | `slate-900` |
| Text | `$color-text` | `slate-50` |
| Muted | `$color-text-muted` | `slate-400` |
| Border | `$color-border` | `slate-700` |
| Accent | `$color-primary` | `cyan-400` |
| Accent hover | `$color-primary-hover` | `cyan-300` |
| Accent soft | `$color-primary-soft` | `cyan-950` |
| On accent | `$color-on-primary` | `slate-950` |
| Glow | `$color-accent-glow` | `cyan-500` |
| Danger / Success / Warning | rose-400 / emerald-400 / amber-400 (+ `*-950` soft) |

## Rules

- Prefer `$color-*` / semantic `--color-*` over raw `slate-*` / `cyan-*` in components.
- Primary CTAs: `$color-primary` fill + `$color-on-primary` text (never light text on cyan).
- Surfaces stay dark; use cyan sparsely for links, focus, active nav, and primary actions.
- Soft backgrounds for alerts/badges use `*-soft` tokens (`*-950`), not light `*-50` tints.
- Atmosphere: subtle cyan radial glows on shell/hero only — no purple gradients, no neon glow stacks.
- Avoid: emerald-as-brand, cream/warm paper, purple-indigo themes, white card chrome.

```svelte
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<button class="bg-emerald-700 text-white">Save</button>

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<button class="btn btn-primary">Save</button>
<!-- or SCSS: background: $color-primary; color: $color-on-primary; -->
```
